# PPPC4DM ID -- annihilation spectra tables (Cirelli et al.)
#
# Source:  http://www.marcocirelli.net/PPPC4DMID.html
# Fetched: 2026-08-06 (copied in with the rest of fermi_legacy/)
# Read by: python/fermi_funcs.py::_load_cirelli_table, via config.DATA_DIR
#
# Pinned rather than committed. These are 40 MB of a public, versionless
# literature release, and the repository's rule is that git carries the recipe
# and not the bytes. But "fetch it from the web page" is not a recipe if
# nothing checks what arrived: the tables have no version string, the site
# republishes in place, and a silent swap would move every Fermi limit in
# Part II without changing a filename. The digests below are that check.
#
# The two directories are not alternates. AtProduction_all/ has electroweak
# corrections applied and 179 energies per mass; AtProductionNoEW_all/ has
# neither, at 180 energies. _load_cirelli_table hardcodes those two row counts
# to reshape the flat table, so a file swapped between the two trees would
# reshape without error and silently mis-map energies onto masses. Both are
# pinned for that reason, and all seven particle tables in each, not just the
# gammas pair the Fermi path currently requests -- the loader takes `particle`
# as an argument and any of them is one call away.
#
# To re-pin: re-fetch, update the digests here, and expect
# tests/test_pppc4dm_pin.py to fail until you do -- that failure is the point.

